Eric Wright wrote:
> Kwirq wrote:
>
> > Is there any particular rhyme or reason to the way nethack presents the 
> > contents of bags of holding and such when you end the game? It would be 
> > really nice if it sorted the items into categories: amulets, weapons, 
> > armour, etc.
>
> > Ditto for the vanquishes monsters: maybe uniques and then by class, or 
> > something. I notice that there _is_ some kind of order in the monster 
> > list, but I can't quite grok how it works.
>
> The relevant code from end.c is 
> 
> Sprintf(buf, "Contents of %s:", the(xname(box)));
> putstr(tmpwin, 0, buf);
> putstr(tmpwin, 0, "");
> for (obj = box->cobj; obj; obj = obj->nobj) {
>     if (identified) {
>        makeknown(obj->otyp);
>        obj->known = obj->bknown =
>        obj->dknown = obj->rknown = 1;
>     }
>     putstr(tmpwin, 0, doname(obj));
> 
> Since it is just looping through the obj in the container, it's most
> likely some type of FIFO ordering, stacking objects with previously
> stored loot where possible.  Don't hold me to that, though!

FIFO order.  Item most recently put into the bag at the top of the
list.  But items aren't stacked when put into a bag.  Try picking up
20 rocks, putting them in a bag, picking up 20 more, etc.  When there
are 100 rocks in the bag apply it of loot it and see.

In a treasure chest, I've gone so far as removing all of the artifacts
and then putting them back in one by one so they display in the order
I chose.  For a save-the-artifacts-collect-the-whole-set game where I
want to end up with them mostly blessed or sorted to my taste or
whatever.

> The monster list sorts by monster level, then by the order in which
> they are listed in monst.c.  That list is ordered by the ascii
> representation of the monster class (a for ants/bees, b for blobs, c
> for c*trices, etc.),

I always thought that it was by when you killed the first monster in that
calss.  Most recently killed type at the top.  Looks like I was wrong.
Certainly as you go deeper more recently encountered monsters are listed
at the top, but monster level will explain that as easily as order first
killed.

